WEBVTT

00:00:00.014 --> 00:00:03.262
We will start with modularity and standard views.

00:00:03.262 --> 00:00:07.502
Then we will inspect reusable objects and their dependencies.

00:00:07.502 --> 00:00:12.437
After that, we will explore controlled writes and access boundaries.

00:00:12.437 --> 00:00:18.352
Materialized views come next, with a focus on freshness and refresh policy.

00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:24.862
Finally, we will combine views and CTEs into a small reusable analytics layer.

00:00:24.862 --> 00:00:28.687
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:28.687 --> 00:00:34.717
an analytics team exposing a stable reporting view to dashboard users.

00:00:34.717 --> 00:00:40.332
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:44.057
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:44.057 --> 00:00:50.942
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:50.942 --> 00:00:54.462
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:54.462 --> 00:00:58.713
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
